                    <birth when="1788-12-06">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1845-06-17"/>
                    <occupation>writer</occupation>
                    <occupation>Church of England clergyman</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Barham was a writer and Church of England clergyman, founding member of the Garrick Club, contributor to many 
  conservative-minded periodicals, very involved in <title>Bentley's Miscellany</title>, and so a prominent member of London literary 
  culture. Godwin generally sees him 'adv' at the theatre.</p>
                        <p>Another possibility is Thomas Foster Barnham, the physician and classical scholar but his family all seem to be in the West Country during the years
  that Barham appears in the diary (that is, 1824-35) which makes it improbable. He also moves to Exeter in 1830 which further discounts him.</p>
                    </note>
